# slidepack's whole premise is byte-exactness: packing is reproducible to the
# byte, tests assert exact file contents, and testdata/ holds binary fixtures
# whose digests are checked. A checkout that rewrites line endings would break
# all three, and Git for Windows enables core.autocrlf by default.
#
# So: no end-of-line conversion for anything, ever, regardless of a
# contributor's local Git configuration.
* -text

# Mark the binary fixtures as binary as well, so `git diff` shows "Binary files
# differ" instead of pages of mojibake.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.avif   binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.mp4    binary
*.webm   binary
*.mp3    binary
*.pdf    binary
